$\left(a^* b\right)^2=\left(a^* a\right)^*\left(b^* b\right)$ for all $a, b \in G\Rightarrow\left(a^* b\right)^*\left(a^* b\right)=\left(a^* a\right)^*\left(b^* b\right)$ for all $a, b \in Ga^*\left(b^* a\right)^{\star} b=a^*\left(\left(a^* b\right)^{\star} b\right.$
for all $a, b \in G\Rightarrow b^* a=a^* b$ for all $a, b \in G$ \{by cancellation laws\}
$\Rightarrow G$ is abelian.

Given, $a_0=1$
and $a_{n+1}=3 n^2+n+a_n\Rightarrow  a_n=3(n-1)^2+(n-1)+a_{n-1}$
Now, put $n=1,2,3, \ldots, n$ We get,
$a_1=0+a_0=0+1=1\begin{array}{ll}\Rightarrow & a_2=4+a_1 \\ \Rightarrow & a_3=14+a_2 \\ \Rightarrow & a_4=30+a_3\end{array}
........
........
........
$\begin{array}{ll}\Rightarrow & a_{n-1}=3(n-2)^2+(n-2)+a_{n-2} \\ \Rightarrow & a_n=3(n-1)^2+(n-1)+a_{n-1}\end{array}
On adding, we get $a_n=\left(1+4+14+30+\ldots+3(n-1)^2+(n-1)\right)\begin{array}{ll}\Rightarrow & a_n=\Sigma 3\left(n^2+1-2 n\right)+(n-1) \\ \Rightarrow & a_n=\Sigma\left(3 n^2+3-6 n+n-1\right) \\ \Rightarrow & a_n=\Sigma\left(3 n^2-5 n+2\right) \\ \Rightarrow & a_n=3 \Sigma n^2-5 \Sigma+2 \Sigma 1\end{array}
$\Rightarrow  a_n=\frac{3 n(n+1)(2 n+1)}{6}-\frac{5 n(n+1)}{2}+2 n\Rightarrow  a_n=\frac{n}{2}(n+1)\{2 n+1-5\}+2 n\Rightarrow  a_n=\frac{n}{2}(n+1)(2 n-4)+2 n=n(n+1)(n-2)+2 n\Rightarrow  a_n=\left(n^2+n\right)(n-2)+2 n=n^3-2 n^2+n^2-2 n+2 n\Rightarrow  a_n=n^3-n^2 (\because n \geq 0)
